{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793463679839,"sessionID":"ses_e6d3ce8c9ffeJ1xzKXDoULu3JY","part":{"partID":"prt_192c3f969001wPZ0FEPwl4DlAA","sessionID":"ses_e6d3ce8c9ffeJ1xzKXDoULu3JY","messageID":"msg_192c3ef88001Bs01R2N8vY37qp","type":"tool","id":"call_01a192c3f9497391bf0c490f51e47a54","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/fix-2/docs/ADRs/0002-cycle2-scoped-fixes.md"},"output":"Read file /private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/fix-2/docs/ADRs/0002-cycle2-scoped-fixes.md, lines 1-117\n1: # ADR 0002 — Cycle-2 scoped fixes: D-08 exception, analyzer honesty, CacheStore Phase-2, melos status\n2: \n3: - Status: accepted (items 2–4 record fact; item 1 is a conditional grant)\n4: - Date: 2026-10-29\n5: - Partition: p5 repo-hygiene-lows (Halloween TV)\n6: \n7: ## 1. D-08 ports-restructure exception (p4)\n8: \n9: ADR 0001 encodes design D-08 dependency-direction rules\n10: (contracts `<-` adapters; `core_*` never depends on `channel_*`,\n11: `infra_*`, or `kernel_app`). Partition p4\n12: (`orchestrator-cycle-2-part-p4-contracts-playlist-ports`) owns the\n13: contracts/playlist ports restructure.\n14: \n15: Fact (corrected at merged head): p4 **has landed** — commit `7e32d48`\n16: (`cycle-2 part p4-contracts-playlist-ports`), merge `72223a7`\n17: (`cycle-2 merge p4`). The \"no landed diff\" sentence above was true at the\n18: time of writing and is now superseded by this paragraph.\n19: \n20: Verified final p4 edge set (all point in the ADR 0001 direction; grant\n21: satisfied, no amendment needed):\n22: - `channel_api` -> `core_foundation` only;\n23: - `core_playlist` -> `core_foundation` only;\n24: - `core_cache` -> `core_foundation` + `core_playlist` only;\n25: - `core_effects` no longer -> `core_ui` (declared path dependency\n26:   removed; `core_ui` legitimately depends on `core_effects`);\n27: - `infra_firestore` / `infra_settings` -> `channel_api` (adapters consume\n28:   the contracts port; no `core_*`/`channel_*` edge points the wrong way).\n29: \n30: Decision — narrow conditional grant: p4 may relocate port\n31: declarations **among contract packages only**\n32: (`channel_api`, `core_cache`, `core_playlist`, `core_foundation`)\n33: without a new ADR, provided every resulting edge still points in\n34: the ADR 0001 direction. Any edge that would violate the direction\n35: rules (e.g. a `core_*` package depending on a `channel_*`,\n36: `infra_*`, or `kernel_app` package) requires an explicit amendment\n37: here **before** merge. Merge gate: the orchestrator confirms the\n38: final p4 edge set against ADR 0001 §Dependency-direction rules.\n39: \n40: ## 2. `dart analyze`, recorded honestly\n41: \n42: Environment: Flutter 3.47.7 / Dart 3.13.5 (stable), melos 6.3.3.\n43: \n44: - Fresh-checkout root `dart analyze`: **2810 issues**, dominated by\n45:   `uri_does_not_exist` / `undefined_identifier` cascades\n46:   (e.g. `package:flutter/material.dart` unresolvable). Cause: no\n47:   `.dart_tool/` exists in this worktree — per-package\n48:   `flutter pub get` never ran here. ADR 0001's \"No issues found!\"\n49:   is therefore **not reproducible from a fresh checkout**; it\n50:   assumed prior per-package resolution.\n51: - After `flutter pub get --offline` in each touched package,\n52:   `dart analyze packages/core_ui packages/core_effects\n53:   packages/testing_toolkit` reports **8 issues, all info-level\n54:   lints, zero errors/warnings**:\n55:   - `always_use_package_imports` ×4 (`cctv_tile.dart:6,7`,\n56:     `hud_overlay.dart:9`, `signal_lost.dart:6` — relative\n57:     `lib/` imports; pre-existing, outside this batch except the\n58:     `hud_overlay.dart` line, which is left as-is to keep the diff\n59:     minimal);\n60:   - `prefer_const_constructors` ×3 (`core_ui_test.dart:212,214,217`,\n61:     pre-existing);\n62:   - `prefer_final_locals` ×1 (`testing_toolkit.dart:43`,\n63:     pre-existing, file outside this partition).\n64: - Root `dart analyze` stays red until full-workspace resolution\n65:   exists — follow-up for whichever partition lands the root\n66:   pubspec (see §4).\n67: \n68: ## 3. Phase-2 full CacheStore adapter follow-up\n69: \n70: `FakeCacheStore` (`testing_toolkit`) is test-only and not a\n71: production cache:\n72: \n73: - `commit()` trusts the caller-supplied sha256 — it never hashes\n74:   `bytes`;\n75: - `deleteExpired()` clears **everything** and returns the count —\n76:   there is no TTL or expiry policy;\n77: - storage is a process-local `Map`, with no persistence.\n78: \n79: Phase-2 production adapter must: hash bytes on `commit` and\n80: reject mismatches, implement a real expiry policy, and persist\n81: `localRef`s. The `CacheStore` port signature in `core_cache`\n82: stays unchanged, so callers are unaffected.\n83: \n84: ## 4. melos status (probe, then revert)\n85: \n86: - Baseline: melos 6.3.3 refuses to run — `Found a melos.yaml file\n87:   ... but no local installation of Melos` (confirms ADR 0001).\n88: - Probe: added a temporary root `pubspec.yaml` (`name:\n89:   halloween_tv`, explicit `workspace:` list of all 14 members —\n90:   13 `packages/*` + `apps/tv_app` — plus `dev_dependencies:\n91:   melos: ^6.3.3`). `dart pub get --offline` fails with:\n92:   `packages/channel_api/pubspec.yaml is included in the workspace\n93:   from ./pubspec.yaml, but does not have 'resolution: workspace'.`\n94: - Conclusion: **not trivially viable**. Enabling workspaces needs\n95:   `resolution: workspace` in all 14 member pubspecs plus the root\n96:   pubspec — all outside the p5 file list — so the probe file was\n97:   deleted, `melos.yaml` is left untouched, and the `melos *`\n98:   scripts remain aspirational until the workspace owner lands the\n99:   root pubspec + member migrations.\n100: \n101: ## Verification (this partition)\n102: \n103: - `flutter pub get --offline` in `core_ui`, `core_effects`,\n104:   `testing_toolkit`: resolved (pub notes 2 packages with newer\n105:   incompatible versions; resolution itself succeeds).\n106: - `flutter test --no-pub` per package: core_ui 13 passed,\n107:   core_effects 15 passed, testing_toolkit 12 passed.\n108: - `git check-ignore -v apps/tv_app/.env` → ignored\n109:   (`apps/tv_app/.gitignore:46`); root `**/.env*` also covers it.\n110:   `.env.example` is explicitly re-included (`!**/.env.example`)\n111:   and shows as committable (`??`) in `git status`.\n112: - `.env.example` contains placeholder values only; zero secrets.\n113: - `core_effects` no longer declares the `core_ui` path dependency\n114:   (nothing under `packages/core_effects/lib` ever imported it;\n115:   this also removes the declared `core_effects` ↔ `core_ui`\n116:   dependency cycle, since `core_ui` legitimately depends on\n117:   `core_effects`).","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/fix-2/docs/ADRs/0002-cycle2-scoped-fixes.md, lines 1-117\n1: # ADR 0002 — Cycle-2 scoped fixes: D-08 exception, analyzer honesty, CacheStore Phase-2, melos status\n2: \n3: - Status: accepted (items 2–4 record fact; item 1 is a conditional grant)\n4: - Date: 2026-10-29\n5: - Partition: p5 repo-hygiene-lows (Halloween TV)\n6: \n7: ## 1. D-08 ports-restructure exception (p4)\n8: \n9: ADR 0001 encodes design D-08 dependency-direction rules\n10: (contracts `<-` adapters; `core_*` never depends on `channel_*`,\n11: `infra_*`, or `kernel_app`). Partition p4\n12: (`orchestrator-cycle-2-part-p4-contracts-playlist-ports`) owns the\n13: contracts/playlist ports restructure.\n14: \n15: Fact (corrected at merged head): p4 **has landed** — commit `7e32d48`\n16: (`cycle-2 part p4-contracts-playlist-ports`), merge `72223a7`\n17: (`cycle-2 merge p4`). The \"no landed diff\" sentence above was true at the\n18: time of writing and is now superseded by this paragraph.\n19: \n20: Verified final p4 edge set (all point in the ADR 0001 direction; grant\n21: satisfied, no amendment needed):\n22: - `channel_api`