{"type":"text","timestamp":1793464260665,"sessionID":"ses_e6d3ce8c9ffeJ1xzKXDoULu3JY","part":{"id":"prt_192ccd838002sAZWSLHGSfJuBX","sessionID":"ses_e6d3ce8c9ffeJ1xzKXDoULu3JY","messageID":"msg_192ccd151001Ah7vVZ0Mh1YoMS","type":"text","text":"Writing the ADR for host entry and camera layout decisions.","time":{"start":1793464260664,"end":1793464260665}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793464269733,"sessionID":"ses_e6d3ce8c9ffeJ1xzKXDoULu3JY","part":{"partID":"prt_192ccd844001ZQRSwYr5z5zy4A","sessionID":"ses_e6d3ce8c9ffeJ1xzKXDoULu3JY","messageID":"msg_192ccd151001Ah7vVZ0Mh1YoMS","type":"tool","id":"call_01a192ccd7fa7594832561a9accb2476","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# ADR 0003 — Dedicated host entry, camera display cap, and invite/PIN separation\n\n- Status: accepted\n- Date: 2026-10-31\n- Partition: fix-2 apps security + polish (Halloween TV cycle-12)\n\n## 1. Dedicated host entry screen (separate from guest PIN admission)\n\nDecision: the companion boots to a dedicated `HostEntryScreen` (Scan Host\nQR + paste fallback + explicit \"Join as guest\" route) instead of a single\njoin form with a role toggle.\n\nRationale: guest PIN admission is intentionally broad — anyone who can see\nthe TV screen can self-register as a guest. Host administration must never\nbe reachable through the guest PIN or a client-supplied role string, so\nthe two routes stay visibly distinct and the privilege boundary stays\nauditable: host payloads redeem only through `joinHost` (separate phone\nidentity, server-assigned `host` role) while guest payloads register only\nthrough `joinParty`.\n\nConsequences:\n- The host QR carries a server-minted, short-lived invite capability\n  (`inviteToken`) plus a 6-digit `pairingCode` shown next to the QR; both\n  are required by `joinHost`, and a wrong code denies exactly like an\n  unknown invite (generic `FORBIDDEN`, no oracle).\n- The entry screen collects the pairing code in its own field (manual\n  entry authoritative; a code inside a scanned/pasted payload only\n  prefills an empty field — scan/paste parity), validates it locally\n  (6 digits, no network on failure), and surfaces denial as the generic\n  sanitized message only.\n\n## 2. Camera display cap (`cameraCount` key, encoding, default)\n\nDecision: `cameraCount` is a display cap only, persisted through the\nexisting party-scoped `SettingsPort` string key\n(`CctvWallSettingsKeys.cameraCount`) with values `'1'` / `'2'` / `'4'`\n(surrounding whitespace tolerated, raw ints accepted defensively) and a\ndefault of `4` (`kDefaultCctvClipCount`) for anything absent, invalid, or\nunreadable.\n\nRationale: the setting can only ever HIDE cameras, never invent them —\n`cctvEffectiveCount = min(configured, manifest clips)` — while prepare /\nverify / ACK always cover the complete received manifest. Generation\npresets keep producing 4 clips and reduced layouts still ACK the full\nmanifest, so `1`/`2`-camera manifests flow through the real mapping,\ndurable-cache, delivery, and ACK paths. `isSupportedCctvClipCount`\n(1, 2, 4) is the shared gate on both sides; the wall fails closed\n(SIGNAL-LOST/cache state, no `StateError` out of construction) on any\nother manifest length.\n\n## 3. Host-invite vs guest-PIN separation\n\nDecision: the guest QR is `partyId + channelId + role: 'guest'` plus an\noptional six-digit `joinPin`; the HOST QR is `partyId + channelId +\nrole: 'host'` plus `inviteToken + pairingCode`. A PIN-shaped token never\nredeems host access (rejected client-side and by `parseJoinHostInput`),\na host payload never carries a `joinPin`, and client-supplied role\nstrings are ignored — the backend assigns `host` server-side,\ntransactionally, bound to party/channel/expiry.\n\nConsequences: legacy guest payloads without `role` stay parseable\n(role-absent means guest); unknown roles fail visibly; guest payloads\nsubmitted on the host entry (or vice versa) fail before any callable.\n\n## 4. Preview/delivery separation + host revocation\n\nDecision: previews are fresh scoped capabilities per view\n(`getHostVideoPreview` → short-lived signed URLs, never persisted),\nwhile delivery manifests are the only durable playback artifact. Deletion\nis per selected seed id (previews + delivery objects removed, affected\ncurrent manifest revoked, accounting records preserved) behind a\nconfirmation dialog naming the seed(s), reconciled only after\nauthoritative success so failures stay retryable in place.\n\nHost management on the TV (`revokeHostDevice`, TV-only) lists active\nhosts as LABELS ONLY — device ids never render — and revokes by opaque\nid behind a second confirmation naming the label; the row stays until\nthe server confirms.\n","path":"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/fix-2/docs/ADRs/0003-host-entry-and-camera-layout.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: docs/ADRs/0003-host-entry-and-camera-layout.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: docs/ADRs/0003-host-entry-and-camera-layout.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false,"state":{"itemId":"fc_01a192ccd7fa7594832561a9accb2476"}},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# ADR 0003 — Dedicated host entry, camera display cap, and invite/PIN separation\\n\\n- Status: accepted\\n- Date: 2026-10-31\\n- Partition: fix-2 apps security + polish (Halloween TV cycle-12)\\n\\n## 1. Dedicated host entry screen (separate from guest PIN admission)\\n\\nDecision: the companion boots to a dedicated `HostEntryScreen` (Scan Host\\nQR + paste fallback + explicit \\\"Join as guest\\\" route) instead of a single\\njoin form with a role toggle.\\n\\nRationale: guest PIN admission is intentionally broad — anyone who can see\\nthe TV screen can self-register as a guest. Host administration must never\\nbe reachable through the guest PIN or a client-supplied role string, so\\nthe two routes stay visibly distinct and the privilege boundary stays\\nauditable: host payloads redeem only through `joinHost` (separate phone\\nidentity, server-assigned `host` role) while guest payloads register only\\nthrough `joinParty`.\\n\\nConsequences:\\n- The host QR carries a server-minted, short-lived invite capability\\n  (`inviteToken`) plus a 6-digit `pairingCode` shown next to the QR; both\\n  are required by `joinHost`, and a wrong code denies exactly like an\\n  unknown invite (generic `FORBIDDEN`, no oracle).\\n- The entry screen collects the pairing code in its own field (manual\\n  entry authoritative; a code inside a scanned/pasted payload only\\n  prefills an empty field — scan/paste parity), validates it locally\\n  (6 digits, no network on failure), and surfaces denial as the generic\\n  sanitized message only.\\n\\n## 2. Camera display cap (`cameraCount` key, encoding, default)\\n\\nDecision: `cameraCount` is a display cap only, persisted through the\\nexisting party-scoped `SettingsPort` string key\\n(`CctvWallSettingsKeys.cameraCount`) with values `'1'` / `'2'` / `'4'`\\n(surrounding whitespace tolerated, raw ints accepted defensively) and a\\ndefault of `4` (`kDefaultCctvClipCount`) for anything absent, invalid, or\\nunreadable.\\n\\nRationale: the setting can only ever HIDE cameras, never invent them —\\n`cctvEffectiveCount = min(configured, manifest clips)` — while prepare /\\nverify / ACK always cover the complete received manifest. Generation\\npresets keep producing 4 clips and reduced layouts still ACK the full\\nmanifest, so `1`/`2`-camera manifests flow through the real mapping,\\ndurable-cache, delivery, and ACK paths. `isSupportedCctvClipCount`\\n(1, 2, 4) is the shared gate on both sides; the wall fails closed\\n(SIGNAL-LOST/cache state, no `StateError` out of construction) on any\\nother manifest length.\\n\\n## 3. Host-invite vs guest-PIN separation\\n\\nDecision: the guest QR is `partyId + channelId + role: 'guest'` plus an\\noptional six-digit `joinPin`; the HOST QR is `partyId + channelId +\\nrole: 'host'` plus `inviteToken + pairingCode`. A PIN-shaped token never\\nredeems host access (rejected client-side and by `parseJoinHostInput`),\\na host payload never carries a `joinPin`, and client-supplied role\\nstrings are ignored — the backend assigns `host` server-side,\\ntransactionally, bound to party/channel/expiry.\\n\\nConsequences: legacy guest payloads without `role` stay parseable\\n(role-absent means guest); unknown roles fail visibly; guest payloads\\nsubmitted on the host entry (or vice versa) fail before any callable.\\n\\n## 4. Preview/delivery separation + host revocation\\n\\nDecision: previews are fresh scoped capabilities per view\\n(`getHostVideoPreview` → short-lived signed URLs, never persisted),\\nwhile delivery manifests are the only durable playback artifact. Deletion\\nis per selected seed id (previews + delivery objects removed, affected\\ncurrent manifest revoked, accounting records preserved) behind a\\nconfirmation dialog naming the seed(s), reconciled only after\\nauthoritative success so failures stay retryable in place.\\n\\nHost management on the TV (`revokeHostDevice`, TV-only) lists active\\nhosts as LABELS ONLY — device ids never render — and revokes by opaque\\nid behind a second confirmation naming the label; the row stays until\\nthe server confirms.\\n\",\"path\":\"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/fix-2/docs/ADRs/0003-host-entry-and-camera-layout.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793464260676,"end":1793464269733}}}}
