{"type":"text","timestamp":1793464304737,"sessionID":"ses_e6d3ce8c9ffeJ1xzKXDoULu3JY","part":{"id":"prt_192cd845e001eH1f0hncpIPk0u","sessionID":"ses_e6d3ce8c9ffeJ1xzKXDoULu3JY","messageID":"msg_192cd738800113gbabxFKS0A7y","type":"text","text":"Integration tests gated. Adding README notes on the host flow.","time":{"start":1793464304734,"end":1793464304737}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793464309118,"sessionID":"ses_e6d3ce8c9ffeJ1xzKXDoULu3JY","part":{"partID":"prt_192cd84b5001QyssbwKGz0CkOs","sessionID":"ses_e6d3ce8c9ffeJ1xzKXDoULu3JY","messageID":"msg_192cd738800113gbabxFKS0A7y","type":"tool","id":"call_01a192cd8464742f9c3bd1ecbfcc54ab","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## Playback recovery\n\nPress MENU or hold OK to open the recovery panel. `RETRY CACHED WALL`\nre-verifies the app-private committed files before changing the wall;\n`DISABLE EFFECTS` is saved in SharedPreferences under the current party ID and\nrestored on the next boot. Live manifests are staged and acknowledged before\nactivation, and each changed tile is replaced in sequence so the wall never\nallocates more than four decoders.\n\n## Host QR + guest codes\n\nThe recovery panel links two separately labelled destinations:\n\n- `HOST QR`: the TV mints a short-lived host invite (`createHostInvite`)\n  and shows exactly one QR plus the 6-digit pairing code beside it. Both\n  are required on the companion host entry; a wrong code denies exactly\n  like an unknown invite. Below the invite, active hosts are listed by\n  label only (device ids never render) with a confirmed revoke action\n  (`revokeHostDevice`, TV-only).\n- `GUEST CODES`: party/channel scope plus one session QR for guests. The\n  TV device id authorizes the listing request but is never displayed.\n\nAn unsupported manifest clip count (anything but 1, 2, or 4) fails\nclosed to a SIGNAL-LOST/cache state instead of throwing during\nconstruction; a held D-pad direction keeps traversing through key\nrepeats while held select never retriggers the hero.","oldString":"## Playback recovery\n\nPress MENU or hold OK to open the recovery panel. `RETRY CACHED WALL`\nre-verifies the app-private committed files before changing the wall;\n`DISABLE EFFECTS` is saved in SharedPreferences under the current party ID and\nrestored on the next boot. Live manifests are staged and acknowledged before\nactivation, and each changed tile is replaced in sequence so the wall never\nallocates more than four decoders.","path":"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/fix-2/apps/tv_app/README.md"},"output":"Edited apps/tv_app/README.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"apps/tv_app/README.md","patch":"Index: apps/tv_app/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- apps/tv_app/README.md\n+++ apps/tv_app/README.md\n@@ -62,4 +62,22 @@\n `DISABLE EFFECTS` is saved in SharedPreferences under the current party ID and\n restored on the next boot. Live manifests are staged and acknowledged before\n activation, and each changed tile is replaced in sequence so the wall never\n allocates more than four decoders.\n+\n+## Host QR + guest codes\n+\n+The recovery panel links two separately labelled destinations:\n+\n+- `HOST QR`: the TV mints a short-lived host invite (`createHostInvite`)\n+  and shows exactly one QR plus the 6-digit pairing code beside it. Both\n+  are required on the companion host entry; a wrong code denies exactly\n+  like an unknown invite. Below the invite, active hosts are listed by\n+  label only (device ids never render) with a confirmed revoke action\n+  (`revokeHostDevice`, TV-only).\n+- `GUEST CODES`: party/channel scope plus one session QR for guests. The\n+  TV device id authorizes the listing request but is never displayed.\n+\n+An unsupported manifest clip count (anything but 1, 2, or 4) fails\n+closed to a SIGNAL-LOST/cache state instead of throwing during\n+construction; a held D-pad direction keeps traversing through key\n+repeats while held select never retriggers the hero.\n","status":"modified","additions":18,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited apps/tv_app/README.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false,"state":{"itemId":"fc_01a192cd8464742f9c3bd1ecbfcc54ab"}},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"## Playback recovery\\n\\nPress MENU or hold OK to open the recovery panel. `RETRY CACHED WALL`\\nre-verifies the app-private committed files before changing the wall;\\n`DISABLE EFFECTS` is saved in SharedPreferences under the current party ID and\\nrestored on the next boot. Live manifests are staged and acknowledged before\\nactivation, and each changed tile is replaced in sequence so the wall never\\nallocates more than four decoders.\\n\\n## Host QR + guest codes\\n\\nThe recovery panel links two separately labelled destinations:\\n\\n- `HOST QR`: the TV mints a short-lived host invite (`createHostInvite`)\\n  and shows exactly one QR plus the 6-digit pairing code beside it. Both\\n  are required on the companion host entry; a wrong code denies exactly\\n  like an unknown invite. Below the invite, active hosts are listed by\\n  label only (device ids never render) with a confirmed revoke action\\n  (`revokeHostDevice`, TV-only).\\n- `GUEST CODES`: party/channel scope plus one session QR for guests. The\\n  TV device id authorizes the listing request but is never displayed.\\n\\nAn unsupported manifest clip count (anything but 1, 2, or 4) fails\\nclosed to a SIGNAL-LOST/cache state instead of throwing during\\nconstruction; a held D-pad direction keeps traversing through key\\nrepeats while held select never retriggers the hero.\",\"oldString\":\"## Playback recovery\\n\\nPress MENU or hold OK to open the recovery panel. `RETRY CACHED WALL`\\nre-verifies the app-private committed files before changing the wall;\\n`DISABLE EFFECTS` is saved in SharedPreferences under the current party ID and\\nrestored on the next boot. Live manifests are staged and acknowledged before\\nactivation, and each changed tile is replaced in sequence so the wall never\\nallocates more than four decoders.\",\"path\":\"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/fix-2/apps/tv_app/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793464304821,"end":1793464309118}}}}
